  "hh_ethnologue_comment": {
    "comment": "Yarumá, a Cariban language of the Xingu subgroup, is missing\n(**hh:e:Levi-Strauss:UXingu**, **hh:ew:GalvaoSimoes:Txikao**). Yaruma is listed as a dialect of Suyá [suy] (a Jê language), presumably because the ethnic group assimilated to the Suyá (**hh:he:VillasBoas:Xingu**),\nbut the original Yarumá, which is attested\n(**hh:ew:GalvaoSimoes:Txikao**), is certainly not a Suyá dialect. See also: Suyá [suy].",
